cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LMX in published work, cite the software and the benchmark sources used by your case."
title: "LMX: JAX-native inductionless liquid-metal magnetohydrodynamics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jorge
    given-names: Rogerio
version: 1.1.3
date-released: 2026-05-01
repository-code: "https://github.com/uwplasma/LMX"
url: "https://lmx.readthedocs.io/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - magnetohydrodynamics
  - liquid metal
  - JAX
  - differentiable simulation
  - fusion engineering
abstract: >-
  LMX is a research code for incompressible, inductionless liquid-metal MHD.
  Its stable surface covers verified fully developed duct flows; extruded,
  turbulent, heat-transfer, and blanket workflows retain explicit research-stage
  labels until their external validation gates pass.
